          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Intel Corporation Investment Policy Committee (Petitioner), the case concerns how to interpret \u201cactual knowledge\u201d under Section 1113(2) of ERISA, which sets a three\u2011year limitations period for breach of fiduciary duty claims."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Intel Corporation Investment Policy Committee (Petitioner)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Intel Corporation Investment Policy Committee (Petitioner), according to Intel Corporation Investment Policy Committee (Petitioner), petitioners argue that the statute requires only that the plaintiff have actual knowledge, not proof of subjective awareness."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8d4bbc74ccf012e795cb289fb7c37d1a601c8c1761f81453e2a472f7039aaf0d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8d4bbc74ccf0-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 34,
              "start": 34
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent, respondents contend that \u201cactual knowledge\u201d means the plaintiff must truly be aware of the breach."
      }
